        "original_id": "cbb33a43-cade-53d1-b6cc-0c5cb93441b2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mark Pavelich\n- Organizations: New York Rangers, Minnesota North Stars, San Jose Sharks, U.S. Olympic hockey team, Soviet Union men's ice hockey team\n- Places: Eveleth, Minnesota, Lake Placid, New York\n- Events: 1980 Winter Olympics, Miracle on Ice\n- Roles: ice hockey forward\n\nFacts:\n- Mark Pavelich was born on February 28, 1958, in Eveleth, Minnesota.\n- The Miracle on Ice was a medal-round game in the men's ice hockey tournament at the 1980 Winter Olympics in Lake Placid, New York.\n- The Miracle on Ice was played between the host United States and the defending gold medalists, the Soviet Union.\n- Mark Pavelich was a member of the 1980 U.S. Olympic hockey team that won the gold medal in the event called the Miracle on Ice.\n- Mark Pavelich is a retired U.S. professional ice hockey forward.\n- Mark Pavelich played 355 regular season NHL games between 1981 and 1992 for the New York Rangers, Minnesota North Stars, and San Jose Sharks.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
